think Read KYRI + RADIANT_STYLE to write in voice, then REMEMBER, the newest session-logs rows, and the itinerary pointers. The live edge is Season G open-media, all green; the newest rung was image/disk.rye (the true round structuring element), and its log named three crux-first siblings: a size-histogram/region-picker over regions, an extended-maxima render, and a TOP-HAT by disk.
think Standfast first: confirmed every living REDS row is closed or released (only #75 rests as custody-gated errata), git clean. So the allocation is free for new constructive work under reds-first.
think Crux-first among the three equals-Lindy siblings: the TOP-HAT by disk. It directly lands the disk's payoff (open_disk/close_disk, the two verbs the disk exists for), completes the arc the disk lap opened, and is a genuine Lindy verb (the classic small-feature/uneven-illumination extractor). It mirrors image/morphology_tophat.rye exactly in shape, diverging only by the ELEMENT (a true disk rather than a square), so learning one is learning both.
think Designed the ISOTROPY crux before coding, by hand: a solid 5x5 bright block. A disk of radius 2 cannot hold the block's square corners (they sit outside the round footprint dx^2+dy^2<=r^2), so erode-by-disk leaves only the block center, dilate-by-disk regrows the 13-cell disk, and open_disk(block,2) rounds the block off -- so white_tophat_disk lights the block's far corner (2,2). A 5x5 SQUARE element opens the same block whole (erode leaves the center, dilate regrows the full 5x5), so morphology_tophat's white top-hat stays blank. The two elements genuinely differ on this one block -- the whole reason a round brush exists. Imported morphology_tophat into the selftest for the direct square contrast, exactly as disk.rye built an explicit square element to contrast its round footprint.
think Ordering safety is structural and element-agnostic: opening is anti-extensive (open_disk <= src) and closing extensive (close_disk >= src) for ANY element, so the per-channel subtract_bytes (identical to morphology_tophat's) never underflows -- the assert high >= low proves it before every write.
obs GREEN on the FIRST metal run, no reds -- the crux values hand-traced before coding held: definition byte-for-byte, speck recovery (bright by white, dark by black), the isotropy crux (disk lights the far corner, square blank, the two not equal), the duality law on a translucent field, a flat field blank both hats, alpha measured like any channel, a QOI round-trip, DiskRadiusTooLarge + EmptySource refusals by name, determinism.
obs Compose not braid: this rung owns only the subtraction; disk owns open_disk/close_disk (routed through structure's general max/min gather), qoi the pixel grid, morphology_tophat the square contrast (selftest only). No new gather, blend, codec, or color.
obs Gates all clean: tame_style_check bans clean, width-check exit 0, plain 7-bit ASCII, living_docs_lint advisory-only GREEN, living_card_ascii_witness GREEN (operator card + REDS pure ASCII). image/README.md gained a Residue (round brush) bullet after the disk entry (docs-sync). REMEMBER repointed single-stranded: live edge and Git nib now name tophat_disk, disk folded to a one-line prior-nib comment (no cairn -- a one-line repoint, no fact lost).
obs Council rota lap deep-read item 4, foundations/20260729-224828_reds-first-and-the-allocation.md -- a red books the remainder of the allocation, and every lantern that fires twice should become a self-halting machine. Applied directly: this lap opened by confirming Standfast clear before any new work, exactly as the law asks, and the module's refusals are self-halting guards rather than lanterns. Noted the doc's own internal citation still reads ../work-in-progress/REDS.md (resolves via the work-in-progress -> crux symlink per REDS #87); it is a dated immutable foundation, not part of this round's work, so left untouched rather than rewritten.
